From 176bd40ebc2269cef4652542360a53bc6f37f5b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:20:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hostpath: block volumes on FreeBSD (md(4) disks, publish as a
 link)

The block access type created its backing file with fallocate, attached
it to a loop device and bind-mounted the device onto the publish target,
through Kubernetes' volumepathhandler, which has no FreeBSD support.

Move these steps behind small helpers. On FreeBSD the file is made with
truncate(2), attached to an md(4) disk in vnode mode (mdconfig, FreeBSD's
loop device; the driver runs privileged), and the publish target becomes
a symbolic link to the disk: nullfs can't mount a device node, and the
kubelet resolves the link on the host. Linux keeps its code.
---
 pkg/hostpath/block_freebsd.go | 97 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 pkg/hostpath/block_other.go   | 51 ++++++++++++++++++
 pkg/hostpath/hostpath.go      | 14 ++---
 pkg/hostpath/nodeserver.go    |  8 +--
 4 files changed, 154 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 pkg/hostpath/block_freebsd.go
 create mode 100644 pkg/hostpath/block_other.go

